# Line endings, pinned to LF in the working tree - and this file exists because its
# absence was measured, not because it is customary.
#
# THE DEFECT IT CLOSES. `core.autocrlf=true` is git's Windows default, and with no
# .gitattributes anywhere in this repository it rewrote every text file to CRLF on
# checkout. installer/verify/bcdverify.cpp reads installer/README.md off the disk and
# looks for "\n## The window\n" and "\n### Modes\n". On a fresh clone those bytes are
# "\r\n## The window\r\n", both needles miss, and the suite reports
#
#     856 checks, 3 failures, VERIFY_FAIL
#
# against 856 and 0 from the committed LF blob - 792 CR bytes in that one file. So
# nobody cloning this repository could reproduce a green suite, and the reason was a
# file that was not here.
#
# THE HARNESS ALSO STOPPED DEPENDING ON THIS. readInstallerReadme() now drops CR as it
# widens, so the needles are true of the content whatever wrote it to disk. Both halves
# are deliberate: a check whose verdict depends on the reader's git configuration is
# reporting the state of a machine rather than the state of the program, and a
# repository whose sources arrive in a different shape than they were written in is a
# repository where the standing "ASCII with LF" constraint is not enforceable by anyone
# who did not set their own git up for it.
#
# eol=lf AND NOT eol=crlf: every source in this project is written, measured and
# committed with LF endings, the build tools are all fine with LF, and the two
# measurement commands the constraints name - `tr -cd '\r' | wc -c` and
# `tr -d '\000-\177' | wc -c` - are run against the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything below is bytes and must never be translated. The PNGs are compared byte for
# byte between rounds - fifty committed captures whose whole purpose is that a
# rendering change shows up as a changed file - so a single translated byte in one of
# them would be a false alarm that costs a round to explain.
*.png  binary
*.PNG  binary
*.ico  binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.sys  binary
*.res  binary
*.obj  binary
*.pdf  binary
